    "title": "Jersey Proud: Make-A-Wish NJ grants boy's wish of traveling to Alaska - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Matt Trapani ,\n2 hours ago\nNews 12 has reported on the great work Make-A-Wish New Jersey does to help sick children.\nUp to 400 wishes are granted yearly for sick children around the state.\nThe organization just completed another one. Antoni was diagnosed with Hypoplastic Left Heart Syndrome. He always wanted to go to Alaska to fish.\nMake-A-Wish New Jersey made it happen. The group says that Antoni “not only fished but also explored the unique culture and nature of the region.”\n“His mom shared that it was a trip they will always remember,” stated a social media post from Make-A-Wish New Jersey.",
